{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/94681-owod-and-videogames-no-not-the-mmorpg","id":94681,"title":"OWoD and videogames! (No, not the MMORPG)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-19T20:51:35-07:00","id":94681,"title":"OWoD and videogames! (No, not the MMORPG)","content":"We seen movies, books and tv shows mentioned in the books...but which videogames you think best represent some of the games. what ever its the atmosphere, characters, story and soundtrack? and No, the VtM and HtR dont count since they are WoD material.<br /> <br /> Silent Hill its the best depiction of a Harrowing there could be on Wraith, concider the plot of silent hill 2 , the creature being spectres and well..as for your shadow...you gotta play and see.<br /> Heavy Rain: Wanna do a dark campaing with no supernatual elements what so ever? there you go :P<br /> Metal Gear: I use metal gear to explain the technology and advancement that the tecnocratic union has. even using the patriots as an example of their power.<br /> Portal 1/2 and Half Life: Technocracy at its best<br /> Grim Fandango: Wanna give a new and refreshing twist to Stygia? check this lucas arts classic.<br /> Dante's inferno: what is down the abysm?well.... i always seen dante as a Doomslayer of some sorts...<br /> Max Payne 1,2 and 3: The Ragnarok, Paradise lost and Burning man wrapped on a gift bag. Make him an Imbued (avenger) or mage (an orphan focused on life and time), but the hard boiled detective, his hallucinations and his personal vendetta against Pent..i mean....Valkyr are a perfect tragic story for the WoD<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T12:36:40-07:00","id":95143,"title":"","content":"This is probably the only video game mentioned in a CWOD book that I can recall: <b>The Secret of Monkey Island</b> was in <b>The Changeling Storyteller's Guide</b>. However, I don't know why they did not mention the sequel (<b>LeChuck's Revenge</b>) in conjunction with the first game. Simply because of <i>that ending</i>... hoo boy.<br /> <br /> <b>Final Fantasy VII</b>: A cyberpunk fantasy with a lot of environmental and corruption issues with it. Very in tune with Werewolf: the Apocalypse or can be used with Mage: the Ascension. Shin-ra Electrical Power Company = Pentex has taken over as a government entity or the Technocracy?<br /> <b>Final Fantasy Tactics (Also known as the War of the Lions)</b>: Dark Ages line: Demon, Inquisitor and anything else in that line. Something seems to be rotten within the church. When the players find the truth of the matter and have to fight Demonic monsters, they later get branded as heretics. <b>Vagrant Story</b>, which is also part of this universe, also works with the Dark Ages line.<br /> <b>Puppeteer:</b> A colorful platformer for the PS3. This one would take place in Changeling: the Dreaming as you have to deal with a unseelie bear pooka that has taken over a Lunar realm.<br /> <b><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Folklore_%28video_game%29\" target=\"_blank\">Folklore</a>:</b> Another game that's Changeling: the Dreaming-like.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised you didn't mention the Persona games, which is all about dealing with one's &quot;Shadow&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T12:51:26-07:00","id":95149,"title":"","content":"The World Ends With You was really, really good. It's an RPG that was released on the Nintendo DS and kater got a (surprisingly good) iOS port. You play as Neku, a dead, amnesiac teenager in the fashion district of Tokyo who is unwilling cast into the supernatural Reaper's Game; survive seven days, and you get to come back to life. It's a lot of fun and the story is fantastic Wraith fodder, revolving around what truly matters to people and how important accepting yourself is. (The monsters are animal-graffiti hybrids called Noise that flock to negative human emotion; they're a nice visual option for Spirits). The soundtrack is ace, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T13:13:41-07:00","id":95169,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Long, long ago there was this medieval tactical adventure game called <i>Darklands</i>. Anytime Dark Ages is brought up, I always think of that game.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T18:47:00-07:00","id":95325,"title":"","content":"Was thinking on Hitman and assassins creed as Euctanathos. I mean the leaps of faith MUST BE COINCIDENTAL MAGIC! and the whole idea of killing those who something something dark side and rule mankind","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T20:51:29-07:00","id":95383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/94681-owod-and-videogames-no-not-the-mmorpg?p=95325#post95325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was thinking on Hitman and assassins creed as Euctanathos. I mean the leaps of faith MUST BE COINCIDENTAL MAGIC! and the whole idea of killing those who something something dark side and rule mankind</div> </div> </div> </div>Take the writing in the original <i>Assassin's Creed</i> (i.e. the only one with a story worth a damn) and you have a pretty nice view of the core philosophical dispute between the Traditions and the Technocracy, with all the moral ambiguity I so adore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T07:27:18-07:00","id":95602,"title":"","content":"<b>Castlevania Series: </b>May be a bit of a stretch here but the series can be a fine example on most of the Hunters<br /> <br /> <b>DevilMayCry Series: </b>I find this game series to give a pretty good idea of what it's like to play a Fallen.<br /> <br /> <b>Otogi: </b>Good idea of what a Kuei Jin would be like if they had no demon side to them.<br /> <br /> <b>Gungrave:</b> A good feel on how the Syndicate in Mage roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Soul Calibur: </b>Shows just how devastating the power of an Earthbound can be in the case of Soul Edge<br /> <br /> <b>Dark Souls:</b> I like to think the Abyss in WoD is very similar to the one in Dark Souls. Virtually nothing but pitch blackness that twists anything ti comes in contact with into a Vile reflection of it's former self.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T08:37:00-07:00","id":95668,"title":"","content":"OK, heres a far stretch.......Would The Sims be how the Weaver plays around with humans?.<br /> <br /> Ghostmaster is clearly wraith, F.E.A.R i belive woudl be New World Order the game.<br /> <br /> And would super mario brothers be a Quest from an avtar on the Horizon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T11:33:24-07:00","id":95800,"title":"","content":"Could be, remember when the Weaver takes over, it makes drones.<br /> <br /> I also see Super Mario Brothers as two normal humans being dropped into in the far dreaming in a realm called the Mushroom Kingdom. Seeing as Koopa/Bowser does count as a dragon.<br /> <br /> If you want two more Mage inspired games:<br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beyond_Good_%26_Evil_%28video_game%29\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Beyond Good and Evil</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Psychonauts\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Psychonauts</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T14:01:28-07:00","id":96524,"title":"","content":"There is this really badass game I found where you play a Doomslayer descending into the labyrinth to hunt specters and collect Oboli! I think its called Pacman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T14:12:46-07:00","id":96531,"title":"","content":"How about Amnesia: Dark Descent? That game gives me some solid World of Darkness vibes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T08:07:58-07:00","id":96887,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/94681-owod-and-videogames-no-not-the-mmorpg?p=96524#post96524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is this really badass game I found where you play a Doomslayer descending into the labyrinth to hunt specters and collect Oboli! I think its called Pacman.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> BUHAHAHAHAHA! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T22:28:57-07:00","id":98961,"title":"","content":"Wraith fans might want to check out the upcoming Murdered: Soul Suspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T01:22:28-07:00","id":99020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/94681-owod-and-videogames-no-not-the-mmorpg?p=98961#post98961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraith fans might want to check out the upcoming Murdered: Soul Suspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me wish I had a good computer or a console less than 13 years old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1082-nfi","name":"NFI","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T22:47:42-07:00","id":103853,"title":"","content":"On the most modern level, Beyond: Two Souls is extremely World of Darkness in it's story.<br /> <br /> The Suffering, one of my favorite horror games, is great inspiration for spectres and lunatic wraiths.<br /> <br /> Bioshock's Andrew Ryan as a rogue Son of Ether works out quite well.<br /> <br /> The Assassin's Creed series deals with long running historical conspiracies with fantastic origins. II and IV are personal favorites.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T02:57:47-07:00","id":109134,"title":"","content":"Bloody Roar, just for the shapeshifting fighters. Everyone picks the Werebunny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T06:25:28-07:00","id":109234,"title":"","content":"A lot of my oWoD Vampire games ended up playing a bit like Saints Row series: balls out action, grabbing power by whatever means necessary. I think GTA V could be stretched to portray vampires doing what they have to do to survive. The criminal underworld has always been my main inspiration for vampire games anyways. Howabout Alan Wake? That's a very WoD game right there!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T13:05:13-07:00","id":109573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/94681-owod-and-videogames-no-not-the-mmorpg?p=109134#post109134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloody Roar, just for the shapeshifting fighters. Everyone picks the Werebunny.</div> </div> </div> </div>First two games were good, then the much later games were just broken and very unbalanced.<br /> I don't know if there will ever be a re-boot, but it seems Konami bought out Hudson Soft, so who knows.<br /> <br /> How about Jak II (<i>Jak and Daxter series</i>)? That is what happens to your previous lighthearted franchise when you hire Amy Hennig from the Legacy of Kain series to work on it. Haven is a very dark and gloomy city for sure. And Jak is now capable of shapeshifting (Ahroun auspice for sure).<br /> <br /> And I'm surprised that the Legacy of Kain (<i>Very V:tM</i>) video game series hasn't been brought up in the thread until now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T17:19:43-07:00","id":109727,"title":"","content":"I've got a series that shares some themes and ideas with Orpheus and WtO to a lesser extent. I've actually mentioned it before in the GtSE section of the old WW forums, the Blackwell series from indie developer Wadjet Eye Games. It's a point-and-click adventure game in the vein of the old classics, Day of the Tentacle, the Dig, Sam and Max, Monkey Island. Even keeping the older early 90's era graphics so you don't need a powerful PC to run it.<br /> <br /> The series revolves around Rosa Blackwell, who after her aunt's death discovers the family legacy, a ghost named Joey Malone and a duty to find wayward, restless ghosts and help them accept their deaths and move on. As of this moment there are four games out and available on Steam while the fifth and final game, The Blackwell Epiphany is coming out at the end of this month. Got a great trailer for it too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WAK_CcCDE84&amp;list=UUTEXraekSXc94cD3FXLfR9w\" data-code=\"WAK_CcCDE84\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/WAK_CcCDE84/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T18:27:51-07:00","id":109747,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y18h6J1RPdI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y18h6J1RPdI</a> WHY THIS DEMON THE FALLEN GAME WAS CANCELLED!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T10:48:48-07:00","id":110167,"title":"","content":"This may show my age, but <b>Parasite Eve</b> always made me think of hunting Fomori! And there is the Bloody Roar series... thank goodness WW never made werebunnies. <b>Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</b> for the Dark Age Vampire fans (not the sequels!)<br /> <br /> And let's not forget the original <b>Resident Evil</b> games, just for the horror of what's going to jump out at you if you're human.<b> inFamous</b> if you want to be a mage with LOTS of paradox, <b>Limbo</b> for our angsty Wraith friends, and <b>Scibblenauts</b> for Changelings, because lets face it if my 10 year old loves that game a fairy will too.<br /> <br /> Did anyone ever play the actual Vampire game? I had a friend lend it to me and I just could not get into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2693-agentunicorn","name":"AgentUnicorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T12:23:07-07:00","id":110215,"title":"","content":"Werebunnies.....let me say this.. NEVER RUN A CAMPAING OF WTA TO OTAKUS !!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T13:13:51-07:00","id":110247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentUnicorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/94681-owod-and-videogames-no-not-the-mmorpg?p=110167#post110167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may show my age, but <b>Parasite Eve</b> always made me think of hunting Fomori! And there is the Bloody Roar series... thank goodness WW never made werebunnies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry on age, I was the one who brought up Final Fantasy VII and Final Fantasy Tactics in the thread. Did you know that FF VII, Chrono Trigger, and Parasite Eve were all being worked on around the same time at Square Soft? That's why they share certain ideas with each other (<i>Evil Shapeshifting Virus Alien, Evil Alien, Evil Virus that mutates people, etc.</i>).<br /> <br /> And if you wanted to show age, I could cite <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Altered_Beast\" target=\"_blank\">Altered Beast</a> or <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolfchild\" target=\"_blank\">Wolf Child</a>...<br /> How about <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ScW77tAMOgE\" target=\"_blank\">Solstice</a>, <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mrP90v5N5u4\" target=\"_blank\">Shadowgate</a>, or <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n_rNsK8SqIo\" target=\"_blank\">Uninvited</a> (<i>I remember the Amiga version more than the NES one</i>)?<br /> <br /> If you wanted some goofy inspiration for Hunter, there's <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p0tBqLu_yk0\" target=\"_blank\">Zombies ate my Neighbors</a>.<br /> <br /> &quot;WW <i>never made</i> werebunnies....&quot;, <b>NWOD's Changing Breeds</b> would like to say, &quot;Hi!&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T18:04:04-07:00","id":110454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentUnicorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/94681-owod-and-videogames-no-not-the-mmorpg?p=110167#post110167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did anyone ever play the actual Vampire game? I had a friend lend it to me and I just could not get into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got both Bloodlines and Redemption, which you can find on Steam and Good Old Games respectively. I like them both, Bloodlines a little more as it stays closer to the mechanics of VtM and the world is larger and more developed than in Redemption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T11:27:00-07:00","id":110946,"title":"","content":"any good videogame for mage the ascension?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T13:17:43-07:00","id":111022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/94681-owod-and-videogames-no-not-the-mmorpg?p=110946#post110946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">any good videogame for mage the ascension?</div> </div> </div> </div><u>Games already mentioned in the thread itself:</u><br /> <b>Gungrave</b>: See Goblin404's post.<br /> <b>Beyond Good and Evil</b>: A female Tradition mage snooping around the Technocracy and trying not to get caught in the process.<br /> <b>Psychonauts</b>: Goofy, but deals a lot with exploring other people's minds.<br /> <b>Bioshock</b>: See Wolfgar's post. See the whole series as well, as the Society of Ether would love the world in Infinite. <br /> <b>inFamous</b>: See Agent Unicorn's post.<br /> <b>Solstice</b>: Main character is a Mage that has to stop a Nephandi.<br /> <b>Shadowgate</b>: You have to stop a Nephandi from summoning an evil spirit and have to deal with creatures/minions within.<br /> <br /> <u>Some other games not mentioned yet with mages or at least a cWOD Mage vibe:</u><br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loom_%28video_game%29\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Loom</b></a><br /> <b><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gabriel_Knight\" target=\"_blank\">Gabriel Knight</a></b><br /> <br /> I just forgot about Spoony's Let's Play of <b>Phantasmagoria 2: A Puzzle of Flesh</b>. Now that's defiantly a Pentex inspired game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T01:59:37-07:00","id":111955,"title":"","content":"<b>The Darkness 1 (and 2 to a lesser extent): </b>Jackie Estacado is the embodiement of a Lasombra, between the shadowy minions, abyssal powers, and overall attitude. Great games with a noir atmosphere and a very bittersweet story. I also highly recommend the comic series of the same name alongside Witchblade, all great reads even if you haven't given them a go before.<br /> <b>Nosferatu: The Wrath of Malachi: </b>A young man turned slipshod novice hunter when he finds him and his family in the lair of an Eastern European Tzimisce lord that plans on turning them into his minions. (Underrated gem here that never got that much publicity).<br /> <b>Fatal Frame series: </b>Japanese Wraith-like horror.<br /> <b>Planescape: Torment:</b> Good lord, just look it up. Fantastic storytelling in a very dated game, but it captures the twisted nature of WoD pretty damn well. <br /> <b>Deus Ex series (not so much 2):</b> Conspiracies, technological advancement, cybernetic-augmentations and top-tier storytelling.<br /> <b>Bloodrayne (1, 2, and Betrayal): </b>Hot, scantily-clad femme fatale vampire sexbomb as a protagonist alongside cheesy and campy writing and very violent hack n slashing. The movies are so damn terrible it hurts though, it's like they asked a teenager to do it for a school project, I wouldn't even say half-assed, it is like no ass at all. But the games are good, but full of fanservice.<br /> <b>Call of Cthulu: Dark Corners of the Earth: </b>For the love of all that is unholy, this great horror game is quintessentially Lovecraftian, play it if you like horror. Hell, play it even if you don't like horror. <br /> <br /> While it may not be a game: <b>Hellblazer</b> is also a great read for anyone looking for a good dark comic fix, featuring Constantine, the JL: Dark member that had his own movie with Keanu Reeves. DC recently picked up the rights to it and is making their own new run of Constantine soon. Pretty great stuff worthy of mentioning. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cAnd those who were seen dancing were thought to be insane by those who could not hear the music.\u201d - Friedrich Nietzsche</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/812-datura","name":"Datura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T20:43:13-07:00","id":166502,"title":"","content":"i think &quot;The Wolf Among Us.&quot; would be a great example for Changeling, and &quot;The Walking Dead&quot; (the good videogame, not the crappy FPS) is about a defender looking for redemption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T22:49:53-07:00","id":166644,"title":"","content":"Wraith-like Flash Game: The Dead Case. Basic point and click adventure game.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.newgrounds.com/portal/view/173654\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.newgrounds.com/portal/view/173654</a><br /> <br /> Also, I have only played one game in the series, but Legacy of Kain: Soul Reaver had me imagining what antediluvian vampire society might have been like in Enoch. Plus, the main character becomes a wraith. I can't vouch for any other installations in the series...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T01:24:51-07:00","id":167677,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\">Indigo Prophecy (AKA Fahrenheit) is a good example, the mysticism, conspiracy and horror all go a long way to make a very WOD like feel.<br /> <br /> Vagrant Story really depicts the WOD well, (albeit in a Renaissance like setting with strong Mage elements) and everything said about Indigo Prophecy applies to this game as well.<br /> <br /> Heavy Rain (as said above) demonstrates a very believable situation which would not be unusual in the WOD and tells a FANTASTIC story.<br /> <br /> Planescape Torment showcases a dark and fantastic umbral realm which could be used in a Mage game, I can honestly say the game is amazing and still worth playing to this day.<br /> <br /> I know it's not a game but Spawn the Animated series deserves a mention for how great it is and I really wanted people on the forum to know it's a source of inspiration worth checking out.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T17:15:41-07:00","id":168394,"title":"","content":"I am very surprised that no one has mentioned Geist for the Gamecube. This game is great inspiration for Orpheus and Wraith. You play as a soul separated from its body and you have to get it back through the use of possession of people and artifacts. It also includes some elements of Demon as well. Very under estimated first person shooter with the possession mechanic.<br /> <br /> Did anyone mention Eternal Darkness: Sanity's Requiem? Also for Gamecube. More Call of Cthulhu than World of Darkness, but still some great stuff there especially with the sanity mechanic and the &quot;hallucinations&quot; that result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If people were meant to run around naked, they would be born that way.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1286-nikuchan","name":"Nikuchan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T21:21:59-07:00","id":168592,"title":"","content":"never hear of geist before...<br /> <br /> Ok..:What about Hotline miami <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T06:07:27-07:00","id":168837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class